<h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-left font-display text-blue-750 sm:text-3xl text-balance">2. Assessment as learning: Active tasks</h2>
<p>
Combining learning tasks with assessment tasks ensures that students will focus on the learning. 

<strong>Why?</strong>
Because students are efficient. Assessment tasks are the focus of student effort and non-assessed learning tasks are generally ignored. 
<p>Examples that illustrate the point:</p>

<img src="/public/MATTERImages/examplesOfCombinedTasks.png" />

Learning resources/materials/opportunities are provided in whatever manner you prefer (textbooks, websites, video lessons, in person lectures, workshop activities, etc.) for students to refer to when attempting the tasks. MATTER does not prescribe how you must present your content.
</p>

